OpenNCALayer is an independent reimplementation of the NCALayer protocol and of the
operations behind it. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the National Certification
Authority of the Republic of Kazakhstan. "NCALayer" and "Kalkan" are used only to describe
compatibility.

oncl-pki embeds, in its `roots/` directory, the public CA certificates of the National
Certification Authority of the Republic of Kazakhstan (production PKI), exactly as the
original NCALayer ships them in `cacerts.jks`. They are public documents distributed for free
use; the rights to the certificates themselves belong to their issuer and are not licensed
under Apache-2.0. Their SHA-256 sums are in the repository's `fixtures/nca/SHA256SUMS`.

oncl-pki's `testing-data/rsa.pk8.der` is a synthetic RSA test key with no value: it
protects nothing and is used only by the `testing` feature's mocks.

The workspace builds oncl-gost and oncl-pki against locally modified copies of the
RustCrypto `streebog` 0.11.0 and `hmac` 0.13.0 crates (additive secret-input variants of
the key-agreement and key-wrap paths; the public-document hash and HMAC paths are unchanged).
Both are MIT OR Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) The RustCrypto Project Developers and Artyom
Pavlov. The modified sources and the full notice are in the repository's `vendor/` and
`NOTICE`; this package does not contain them. The third-party crates of the whole SDK closure
with their licence texts are listed in `THIRD-PARTY.txt` of the oncl-core package.
